The Julian line—"in the flat voice of a man explaining arithmetic"—is observed and specific. That's a person. But the prose around it drifts into convention: "the house kept its silence," "the case closed." It lands in one place, then doesn't sustain. And since this is an ending, I can't tell if the voice was like this all the way through or if this is just what happened to land at the bottom of the page.

